  <h2>Our commitment</h2>
  <p>
    St. Paul's Mission Hospital exists to extend the healing ministry of Christ
    through compassionate, dignified, and high-quality healthcare. This Service
    Charter is our public commitment to every patient, family member, and
    visitor — a written promise of the standards you should expect when you come
    to us.
  </p>
  <blockquote>
    "Whatever you did for one of the least of these brothers and sisters of
    mine, you did for me." — Matthew 25:40
  </blockquote>

  <h2>Our pledge</h2>
  <p>We will:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Receive every patient with respect, dignity, and compassion — regardless
      of faith, tribe, gender, age, disability, or ability to pay.
    </li>
    <li>
      Provide safe, competent, and ethical care aligned with national clinical
      guidelines and Catholic moral teaching.
    </li>
    <li>
      Explain your condition, treatment options, and costs in clear language
      before asking for your consent.
    </li>
    <li>
      Protect your privacy and the confidentiality of your health information.
    </li>
    <li>Respond to emergencies promptly, 24 hours a day, 7 days a week.</li>
    <li>
      Treat your family and visitors with courtesy and provide them with clear
      information about your care.
    </li>
    <li>
      Listen to your concerns and resolve complaints fairly, transparently, and
      without delay.
    </li>
  </ul>

